# Data — never tracked; fetched from Kaggle.
# Leading slash anchors this to the repo root, so it does not also swallow src/pcbi/data/.
#
# ...except the manual pairing. It is hours of a person deciding which two photographs show the
# same physical component, it cannot be regenerated from anything (no automatic method could
# reproduce it — see reports/grouping_*.md), and it is a few KB of readable JSON. Everything else
# under data/ can be re-derived from the download; this cannot.
#
# Git will not look inside an excluded directory, so re-including one file means excluding and
# re-including each level down to it by hand. `/data/*` rather than `/data/` is what makes that
# possible at all.
#
# ...and the frozen split, for a related reason. A split whose entire purpose is that every run
# uses the same one cannot live only on the laptop that generated it — Kaggle clones this repo to
# train. `manifest_meta.json` rides along because the split hash it records is what a run logs to
# prove which split it used. Both are small; the crops they point at are not tracked.
/data/*
!/data/interim/
/data/interim/*
!/data/interim/tag_pairs.json
!/data/splits/
/data/splits/*
!/data/splits/*.csv
!/data/manifest_meta.json

# Secrets
.env

# Model weights and checkpoints
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# Experiment tracking / run outputs
wandb/
/outputs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# qa reports
/reports/qa/
# Note: uv.lock and reports/ are deliberately NOT ignored — both are committed.

# Claude Code local settings — machine-specific permissions, not shared project config.
.claude/settings.local.json
